  <regions type="content">
    <region left="18" top="9" width="379" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">OptimWrapper - complete solver reference (CAS-defined problems)</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="45" width="76" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="false">2026-10-24</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="81" width="477" height="203" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">OptimWrapper - every solver, user-defined problems</p>
    <p bold="true">GUID 3c9f7e0a-c2b1-4eae-ab68-9ea2c518c510, v1.0.0.0 (OptimLib 3.1.3 bridge).</p>
    <p bold="true">The plugin ships NO built-in test problems: every objective / constraint / system</p>
    <p bold="true">below is defined here in SMath CAS. Solver result layout: [x1; ...; xn; f; iterations; ok]</p>
    <p bold="true">  f = el(result, n+1);  iterations = el(result, n+2);  ok = el(result, n+3) (1 = converged).</p>
    <p bold="true">All values are unitless. DE/PSO take explicit box bounds (p_min, p_max).</p>
    <p bold="true">Run Calculate All (Ctrl+Shift+F9) if values are not filled in on open.</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="324" width="503" height="533" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">1. The 13 optimisation algorithms</p>
    <p bold="true">LOCAL DETERMINISTIC - unconstrained scalar objective f(x):</p>
    <p bold="true">  0 bfgs     Quasi-Newton (BFGS inverse-Hessian update + line search); robust default.</p>
    <p bold="true">  1 lbfgs    Limited-memory BFGS: low memory, good for many variables.</p>
    <p bold="true">  2 cg       Nonlinear conjugate gradient: little memory; needs a good line search.</p>
    <p bold="true">  3 gd       Gradient descent (steepest descent): simple; slow/diverges with a fixed step.</p>
    <p bold="true">  4 newton   Newton with a numerical Hessian: fast near a minimum, O(n^2) memory.</p>
    <p bold="true">  5 nm       Nelder-Mead simplex: derivative-free; robust but slow in high dimension.</p>
    <p bold="true">GLOBAL STOCHASTIC - population 200, require bounds:</p>
    <p bold="true">  6 de       Differential evolution: mutation/crossover/selection global search.</p>
    <p bold="true">  7 de_prmm  DE with pro-active mutation: extra diversity to avoid premature convergence.</p>
    <p bold="true">  8 pso      Particle swarm: particles follow personal/global bests.</p>
    <p bold="true">  9 pso_dv   PSO with differential variation: more explorative, noisier.</p>
    <p bold="true">CONSTRAINED:</p>
    <p bold="true"> 10 sumt     Sequential Unconstrained Minimisation (penalty) for ci(x) &lt;= 0.</p>
    <p bold="true">ROOT FINDING - square system F(x) = 0:</p>
    <p bold="true"> 11 broyden     Broyden quasi-Newton root finder (secant update of the Jacobian).</p>
    <p bold="true"> 12 broyden_df  Broyden dual-form variant (same goal, different update).</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
    <region left="18" top="1017" width="475" height="23" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
      <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
        <content>
    <p bold="true">2. Problems defined in SMath CAS (objectives, a constraint system, two root systems)</p>
    </content>
      </text>
    </region>
